---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const seo = {
  title: "How to Calculate Your Total Net Worth in India (2026) | Arthavi",
  description: "Step-by-step formula to calculate your personal and family net worth in India. Assets, liabilities, liquid vs illiquid wealth, and free tracking.",
};

const schema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": seo.title,
      "description": seo.description,
      "datePublished": "2026-11-09",
      "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Arthavi Editorial Team" }
    }
  ]
});
---
<Layout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  keywords="how to calculate net worth india, personal net worth formula india, total net worth calculator"
  schema={schema}
  breadcrumb={{
    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Blog", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/" },
      { name: "Calculate Net Worth India", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/calculate-net-worth-india/" }
    ]
  }}
>

<main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem); padding-bottom: 5rem;">
  <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>How to Calculate Your Total Net Worth in India (2026 Guide)</h1>
    <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      Your net worth is the single most accurate scorecard of your financial health. Tracking it over time tells you whether your income is successfully translating into lasting family wealth.
    </p>

    <h2>The Fundamental Formula</h2>
    <div style="background: rgba(99,102,241,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(99,102,241,0.25); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; text-align: center; margin: 2rem 0;">
      <span style="font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; color: #a78bfa;">Net Worth = Total Assets − Total Liabilities</span>
    </div>

    <h2>1. What Counts as Assets in India?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Liquid Financial Assets:</strong> Mutual funds, Demat stocks, bank savings, Fixed Deposits (FD), and Recurring Deposits (RD).</li>
      <li><strong>Retirement &amp; Tax-Advantaged Funds:</strong> EPF, VPF, PPF, and National Pension System (NPS).</li>
      <li><strong>Precious Metals:</strong> Physical 24K/22K gold, silver, Sovereign Gold Bonds (SGB), and digital gold.</li>
      <li><strong>Physical Property:</strong> Residential flats, commercial plots, and land (market valuation).</li>
      <li><strong>Specialized Investments:</strong> SEBI SIFs and AIFs for accredited HNI investors.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. What Counts as Liabilities?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Outstanding home loan principal balance</li>
      <li>Vehicle / car loans</li>
      <li>Personal loans &amp; education loans</li>
      <li>Unpaid credit card statements</li>
    </ul>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin: 3rem 0;">
      <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/register" class="btn btn-primary" style="padding: 1rem 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 1rem;">Track Net Worth on Arthavi</a>
      <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/demo" class="btn btn-demo" style="padding: 1rem 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem;">Try Demo</a>
    </div>

  </article>
</main>

</Layout>
